x86_64-windows  a virtual base is laid out by a vbtable on this ABI, not by a vbase_offset in the vftable, and none of it has been measured against cl - the lag virtual-base-diamond.notarget records at length. This case is refused before it reaches the question it asks, and by the same now-inaccurate message that one describes: `'Dia' has virtual functions in a base that is not the first`, which fires because hasVptr() is `polymorphic() || hasVirtualBase()` and Dia has no virtual function at all. What this case measures - which constructor the most-derived class calls for a virtual base, and with what arguments - is an Itanium question until the Microsoft layout lands.
